20	/**
21	 * The panel's shell: a pinned identity hero, a pinned tab rail, and one tab.
22	 *
23	 * NAVIGATION IS CONSOLIDATED from the thirteen tabs this replaced. Mods and
24	 * Plugins were two views of the same catalogue filtered by keyword, so they are
25	 * one tab with sub-tabs. The three Minecraft-only tabs are folded into the
26	 * section they belong to rather than appearing and disappearing from the rail
27	 * depending on which game you opened: Commands sits under Console (it is a
28	 * command reference for the console), History under Players, and Worlds under
29	 * Backups (they are save directories).
30	 *
31	 * The tab also lives in the URL properly now. The old shell wrote `?tab=` with
32	 * `history.replaceState`, which meant the browser back button skipped the whole
33	 * panel and a link to a tab could not be shared — and two worker notifications
34	 * deep-link into tabs, one of them to a `?tab=game settings` key that never
35	 * existed.
36	 */
